claims all twelve results. Positive nonintegers, zero-adjacent positives,
integer inputs and negative nonintegers remain. Combining the two sources
is justified by their identical floor-evaluation task, not a quota. Whole-vector
recognition loses independent written production and can use valid elimination;
it does not turn the source into isolated blank/cell clicks.
redundancy: PASS. The combined item absorbs the two similar source exercises
instead of asking a second identical floor-vector item. The later example,
inverse-set and decomposition items require different relationships.
answer_leakage: PASS. No stem supplies the correct vector. The negative-number
and integer-endpoint alternatives are definite mathematical claims; their
differences require the floor definition, not internal provenance or wording.

