### V10, source 664, single

task_fidelity: BLOCKED, essential capacity loss. The view keeps both functions,
domain/range/shape/asymptotes, relative order on both half-lines and all three
solution sets. That is substantive exponential-property recognition and its
mathematical assertions can be judged. However the original task explicitly
requires sketching the two graphs and then USING THOSE GRAPHS to obtain the
solutions. Here no graph, candidate drawing or graph-based observation is
present: the learner selects verbal properties and algebraic solution sets.

Drawing production loss alone would not automatically block a faithful
recognition task. The additional decisive loss here is the entire
graph-to-solution operation. A learner can compare (7/4)^x with 1, use
f(0)=g(0)=1 to reject the straight-line claim, and select a fully correct option
without constructing, recognizing or extracting anything from a graph.
The long shared graph-property descriptions in a/b/c do not require converting
an actual crossing or relative height into a set of x values. Thus a student
can answer this item while missing the source's required graphical strategy.
This specific omission destroys an essential component of source 664 rather
than merely failing to prove independent drawing. Verbal property agreement
does not rescue the lost operation.

The losses are: independent sketch production; actual image recognition;
using crossing and relative heights on a graph to solve the equation and both
strict inequalities. They must not be recorded as full graphical coverage.
The block is an intentional content/capacity gap in this view, not an
unreadable original figure, missing scientific data, browser failure or
technical permission HOLD. The original source supplies functions to sketch,
not a hidden diagram; its mathematics remains completely solved.

redundancy: PASS at package level. Exponential comparison is distinct from the
floor/fraction tasks. Within this item the common properties in a/b/c add no
discrimination between those alternatives. All four options also give equation
solution {0}, so equation production is not independently measured. Those are
response limitations, not a reason to alter a correct mathematical claim or
force a different key pattern.
answer_leakage: PASS for the entire choice, with the invariant-equation
limitation explicitly noted. Comparable a/b/c descriptions do not identify
the true full option through wording or length; d's straight-line claim is
mathematically false, not tagged as such. The common {0} component pre-supplies
one subresult but does not reveal the complete valid description. This
whole-item leakage verdict does not remove the task-fidelity block.

